                  \\\
                  0 &amp;&amp;\to &amp;&amp; 2 &amp;&amp; \to &amp;&amp; 4
                  }
          %p or, if preferred, to the fact that
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 4
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 2
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 4
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ×
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 4
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 4
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 4
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S[4](2,4)\times S[4](0,2)\to S[4](0,4)
          %p is to be a simplicial map.
          %p
            A similar phenomenon occurs in higher dimensions. There are two ‘extra faces’ in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 5
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 5
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S[5](0,5)
          %h3#for_other_simplicial_sets For other simplicial sets
          %p
            The description of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S[n]
            works more generally for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerve"} nerve
            of a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/poset"} poset
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            is a poset,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi NP
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S(NP)
            is isomorphic to the simplicially enriched category with the structure
          %ul
            %li
              The objects of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi NP
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S(NP)
              are the elements of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            %li
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-object"} hom-object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi NP
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S(NP)(x,y)
              is the nerve of the poset of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chains"} chains
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo ⊆
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \subseteq P
              with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi min
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \min(S) = x
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi max
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \max(S) = y
            %li Composition is given by taking unions
          %p
            The simplicially enriched categories constructed from spheres and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inner+horns"} inner horns
            also have simple descriptions.
          %p
            For
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi i
                    %mo ,
                    %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≠
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (i,j) \neq (0,n)
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Λ
                      %mi k
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi i
                    %mo ,
                    %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo ∂
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi i
                    %mo ,
                    %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi i
                    %mo ,
                    %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S(\Lambda^n_k)(i,j) = S(\partial \Delta^n)(i,j) = S(\Delta^n)(i,j)
          %p
            For the remaining hom-object, while
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≅
                  %msup
                    %mo □
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S(\Delta^n)(0,n) \cong \square^{n-1}
            is the
            = succeed "-cube," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n-1)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo ∂
                  %msup
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo ∂
                  %msup
                    %mo □
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S(\partial \Delta^n)(0,n) = \partial \square^{n-1}
            is the boundary, and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Λ
                    %mi k
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S(\Lambda^n_k)(0,n)
            further omits the corresponding face.
          %p
            To see this, observe that the nondegenerate simplices of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S(\Delta^n)(0,n)
            are either decomposable (i.e. the product of two or more simplices from other hom-sets) or are the image of a top simplex of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi m
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mi m
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S(\Delta^m)(0,m) \to S(\Delta^n)(0,n)
            for some monomorphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi m
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta^m \to \Delta^n
            preserving top and bottom elements, depending on whether the simplex contains the top vertex
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (0,n)
          %p
            Thus, the decomposable faces of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S(\Delta^n)(0,n)
            are the ones omitting the top vertex
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (0,n)
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta^{n-1} \to \Delta^n
          %h3#for_the_homotopy_coherent_nerve For the homotopy coherent nerve
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Any
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
                gives a simplicially enriched category using the embedding of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
                into
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
                via the usual
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerve"} nerve
                functor. The homotopy coherent nerve of a 2-category considered in this way is, sometimes, called the
                %span.newWikiWord
                  geometric nerve
                  %a{:href => "/nlab/new/geometric+nerve"} ?
                of the 2-category. The
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Duskin+nerve"} Duskin nerve
                of a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bicategory"} bicategory
                is an extension of this construction.
              %p
                A particular case of this nerve is the nerve of a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-group"} 2-group
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} considered as
                a 2-category.
          %h2#Properties Properties
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi sSet
                      %mi Cat
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C \in sSet Cat
                is such that all
                = succeed "s" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-object"} hom-object
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi sSet
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(x,y) \in sSet
                are
                = succeed "es," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complex"} Kan complex
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi N
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N(C)
                is a
                = succeed "/" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+Kan+complex"} weak Kan complex
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-category"} quasi-category
              %p
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo :
                      %mi C
                      %mo →
                      %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : C \to D
                is a morphism of such Kan-complex enriched categories which is a weak equivalence (in the
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+sSet-categories"} model structure on sSet-categories
              %ul
                %li
                  %p the induced functor
                  .maruku-equation
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi Ho
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi f
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo :
                          %mi Ho
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi C
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo →
                          %mi H
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi D
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                          Ho(f) : Ho(C) \to H(D)
                  %p
                    on the ordinary underlying
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category+of+an+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} homotopy categories
                    (obtained by taking hom-wise connected component sets) is
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/essentially+surjective+functor"} essentially surjective
                %li
                  %p its component on each hom-object
                  .maruku-equation
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi f
                            %mrow
                              %mi x
                              %mo ,
                              %mi y
                          %mo :
                          %mi C
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi x
                          %mo ,
                          %mi y
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo →
                          %mi D
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi f
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi x
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ,
                          %mi f
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi y
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                          f_{x,y} : C(x,y) \to D(f(x),f(y))
                  %p
                    is a
                    = succeed "," do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+equivalence"} homotopy equivalence
              %p then its homotopy coherent nerve
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi N
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo :
                      %mi N
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mi N
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      N(f) : N(C) \to N(C)
              %p
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+for+quasi-categories"} weak equivalence of
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-categories"} quasi-categories
              %p
                We may think of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Δ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta[n]
                trivially as a simplicially enriched category. In the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+sSet-categories"} model structure on sSet-categories
                the object
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S[n]
                is a cofibrant replacement of
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Δ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta[n]
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+hom-space"} derived hom-space
                functor
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi N
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi Hom
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Δ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mo •
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo ,
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      N(C) = \mathbb{R}Hom(\Delta[\bullet], C)
                      \\,.
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rigidification+of+quasi-categories"} rigidification of quasi-categories
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relation+between+quasi-categories+and+sSet-enriched+categories"} relation between quasi-categories and sSet-enriched categories
          %h3#comonadic_resolution Comonadic resolution
          %p (To be edited)
          %p
            The use of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S[A]
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            is related to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
            of the homotopy coherent nerve, but is defined using a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comonadic+resolution"} comonadic resolution
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comonad"} comonad
            comes from the adjunction between small categories and directed graphs with distinguished ‘unit’ loops. The ‘forgetful’ part of the adjunction forgets the composition in the category, but remembers that the identity arrows are special. The left adjoint / ‘free’ part of the adjunction takes a directed graph (with distinguished ‘identity’ loops, and forms the free category on the non-identity arrows. As usual, we can form a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comonad"} comonad
            from this and hence form a functorial
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+resolution"} simplicial resolution
            of any small category,
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          %p
            This can also be seen to be a case of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bar+resolution"} bar resolution
            construction, related to the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bar+construction"} bar construction
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
            on directed graphs with distinguished ‘unit’ loops and the small category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is an algebra for this monad.
          %p
            Since the functors involved preserve the identities on the objects of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S[A]
            = succeed "-dimensional" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S[A]
            correspond to a path from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            containing no identity arrows, together with a bracketting of the resulting string having depth
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          %h3#WConstruction
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
            \-Construction of topological operads
          %p By hom-wise precomposition with the singular complex functor
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Sing
                  %mo :
                  %mi Top
                  %mo →
                  %mi sSet
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Sing : Top \to sSet
                  \\,,
          %p
            which is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+functor"} monoidal functor
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} categories
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                  %mo :
                  %mi Top
                  %mi Cat
                  %mo →
                  %mi sSet
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  N : Top Cat \to sSet
                  \\,.
          %p
            As such, it is a special case of the
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Boardman"} Boardman
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Rainer+Vogt"} Vogt
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/W-construction"} W-construction
            for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+operads"} cofibrant replacement of
            topological
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/operads"} operads
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dendroidal+homotopy+coherent+nerve"} dendroidal homotopy coherent nerve
          %p
            In this construction, roughly, for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tree"} tree
            in an operad
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi O
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi e
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e(T) \to [0,1]
            of maps from the set of edges of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            to the topological unit interval.
          %p
            We may restrict this construction to the
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplex"} simplex
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta[n]
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            and then trivially regarded as a
            = succeed "-category." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Top
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta[n]
            is necessarily a linear tree
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo →
                  %mo →
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo →
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \to \to \cdots \to
            of some length
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            and is hence mapped to the topological space of functions
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k \to [0,1]
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [0,1]^k
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+realization"} geometric realization
            of the simplicial cubes
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\Delta[1])^k
            that we saw above.
          %h3#relation_to_quasicategories Relation to quasi-categories
          %p
            As mentioned above, the simplicial or h.c. nerve, together with its
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functor"} left adjoint
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-categories
            given by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-category"} quasi-categories
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicially+enriched+category"} simplicially enriched categories
          %p
            The homotopy coherent nerve extends to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalence
            between the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Joyal+model+structure"} Joyal model structure
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi SSet
                    %mi Joyal
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SSet_{Joyal}
            that models
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-categories"} quasi-categories
            and the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+SSet-categories"} model structure on SSet-categories
          %p See
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relation+between+quasi-categories+and+simplicial+categories"} relation between quasi-categories and simplicial categories
          %p for details.
