          %h3#other_kinds_of_nerves Other kinds of nerves
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerve"} nerve
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Duskin+nerve"} Duskin nerve
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-nerve"} ∞-nerve
            %li
              %p
                %strong homotopy coherent nerve
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-nerve"} dg-nerve
          %h2#history History
          %p
            The original motivation for the introduction of the homotopy coherent nerve is that it provides a neat simplicial formulation of idea of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+coherent+diagram"} homotopy coherent diagrams
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Boardman"} Boardman
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Rainer+Vogt"} Vogt
            in joint work, and then Vogt individually looked at homotopy coherent diagrams. The homotopy coherent nerve was first explicitly defined by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean-Marc+Cordier"} Cordier
            (reference below). He realised that, with a slight modification in the definition, Vogt’s definition of homotopy coherent diagram, indexed by a small category
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SSet
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S[A]
            to the
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SSet
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Top
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerve"} nerve
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            to
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Top
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N(Top)
          %p
            This definition works best when the simplicially enriched category is ‘locally Kan’, in other words it is enriched in the category of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complex"} Kan complexes
            = succeed "-categories" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SSet
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+sSet-categories"} model structure on sSet-categories
          %p
            Cordier and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tim+Porter"} Porter
            (1986) proved that if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is a locally Kan simplicially enriched category then
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N(C)
            is a ‘
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+Kan+complex"}> weak Kan complex
            ’, in other words, a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-category"} quasi-category
            = succeed "\u2018s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Rainer+Vogt"} Vogt
          %p
            In more modern terminology as
            = succeed "es" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complex"} Kan complex
            = succeed "s," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} ∞-groupoid
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} (infinity,1)-category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-categories"} (infinity,1)-categories
            to another, the ‘weak Kan complexes’ or
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-categories"} quasi-categories
          %h2#references_and_literature References and Literature.
          %p The homotopy coherent nerve operation was introduced, explicitly, in
          %ul
            %li#Cordier82
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean-Marc+Cordier"}> Jean-Marc Cordier
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Sur la notion de diagramme homotopiquement cohérent
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.numdam.org/numdam-bin/feuilleter?id=CTGDC_1982__23_1"} numdam:CTGDC_1982__23_1
          %p making a link with earlier work in
          %ul
            %li
              R. D. Leitch,
              = succeed "," do
                %em The homotopy commutative cube
              %strong 2
              9 (1974) 23-29 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1112/jlms/s2-9.1.23"}> doi:10.1112/jlms/s2-9.1.23
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            as well as with
            %a{:href => "#Vogt73"} Vogt (1973)
            and with
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Boardman"}> Michael Boardman
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Rainer+Vogt"} Rainer Vogt
              = succeed "," do
                %em Homotopy invariant algebraic structures on topological spaces
              %strong 347
              Springer (1973) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BFb0068547"}> doi:10.1007/BFb0068547
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            Poof of an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence
            between the category obtained by inverting the ‘levelwise’ homotopy equivalence in a category of diagrams, and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category"} homotopy category
            of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+coherent+diagrams"} homotopy coherent diagrams
          %ul
            %li#Vogt73
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Rainer+Vogt"}> Rainer Vogt
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Homotopy limits and colimits
              %strong 134
              (1973) 11-52 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://eudml.org/doc/171965"}> eudml:171965
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BF01219090"} doi:10.1007/BF01219090
          %p
            and explicit proof that the homotopy coherent nerve of a locally Kan simplicially enriched category is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasicategory"} quasicategory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/outer+horns"} outer horns
            in this quasicategory can be filled:
          %ul
            %li#CordierPorter86
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean-Marc+Cordier"}> Jean-Marc Cordier
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tim+Porter"} Tim Porter
              = succeed "," do
                %em Vogt’s theorem on categories of homotopy coherent diagrams
              %strong 100
              (1986) 65-90 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/S0305004100065877"}> doi:10.1017/S0305004100065877
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://people.math.rochester.edu/faculty/doug/otherpapers/Cordier-Porter.pdf"} pdf
          %p Two other papers are relevant to this:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean-Marc+Cordier"}> Jean-Marc Cordier
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tim+Porter"} Tim Porter
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Maps between homotopy coherent diagrams
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 28
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean-Marc+Cordier"}> Jean-Marc Cordier
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tim+Porter"} Tim Porter
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Fibrant diagrams, rectifications and a construction of Loday
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 67
          %p An elementary discussion of the concept of homotopy coherence forms Chapter V of
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K.+H.+Kamps"}> K. H. Kamps
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tim+Porter"} Tim Porter
              = succeed "," do
                %em Abstract homotopy and simple homotopy theory
          %p
            For the role played by Cordier’s simplicial nerve in the context of relating quasi-categories to simplicially enriched categories as models for
            = succeed "-categories" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andr%C3%A9+Joyal"}> André Joyal
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/The+Theory+of+Quasi-Categories+and+its+Applications"} The Theory of Quasi-Categories and its Applications
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a{:href => "https://lists.lehigh.edu/pipermail/algtop-l/2007q4/000017.html"} Advanced Course on Simplicial Methods in Higher Categories
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://mat.uab.cat/~kock/crm/hocat/advanced-course/Quadern45-2.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/JoyalTheoryOfQuasiCategories.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andr%C3%A9+Joyal"}> André Joyal
                ,
                %em Notes on quasi-categories
                (2008) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.uchicago.edu/~may/IMA/Joyal.pdf"}> pdf
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/JoyalNotesOnQuasiCategories.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
                , section 1.1.5 in:
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} Higher Topos Theory
                (2009)
          %p
            This emphasizes the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functor"} adjunction
            corresponding to the homotopy coherent (“simplicial”) nerve construction.
          %p A review of this latter aspect is also in
          %ul
            %li#Dhand
              %p
                Vivek Dhand,
                %em The simplicial nerve of a simplicial category
                (
                %a{:href => "https://citeseerx.ist.psu.edu/document?repid=rep1&type=pdf&doi=374dc56d9a4352b8f9f71cc12dd7331e9285bb0c"}> pdf
                ,
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Dhand-SimplicialNerve.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                Mitya Boyarchenko,
                %em
                  Notes and exercise on
                  = succeed "-categories" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mn ∞
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
                (
                %a{:href => "http://math.uchicago.edu/~mitya/langlands/quasicategories.pdf"}> pdf
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vladimir+Hinich"}> Vladimir Hinich
                ,
                %em Simplicial nerve in Deformation theory
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0704.2503"}> arXiv:0704.2503
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Denis-Charles+Cisinski"}> Denis-Charles Cisinski
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ieke+Moerdijk"} Ieke Moerdijk
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Dendroidal sets and simplicial operads
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1109.1004"} arxiv/1109.1004
                (a Quillen equivalence for Segal vs. simplicial operads using coherent nerve)
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Emily+Riehl"}> Emily Riehl
                ,
                %em On the structure of simplicial categories associated to quasi-categories, Math. Proc. Camb. Phil. Soc. 150 (2011), 489 - 504.
          %p
            For more references see
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relation+between+quasi-categories+and+simplicial+categories"} relation between quasi-categories and simplicial categories
          %p
            Two query-discussions on terminology and concrete description of the coherent/“simplicial” nerve are archived at nForum
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "http://www.math.ntnu.no/~stacey/Mathforge/nForum/comments.php?DiscussionID=754&Focus=20607#Comment_20607"} here
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Emily+Riehl"}> Emily Riehl
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://golem.ph.utexas.edu/category/2010/04/understanding_the_homotopy_coh.html"} Understanding the homotopy coherent nerve
          %p
            Relating the
            = succeed "-construction" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dwyer-Kan+loop+groupoid"} Dwyer-Kan loop groupoid
          %ul
            %li#MinichielloRiveraZeinalian23
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Emilio+Minichiello"}> Emilio Minichiello
